OL,3,GNEWSATory deputy answers BBC local
OL,4,Aradio questions on bin strike,
OL,5,Aelectoral losses and borrowing
OL,6,
OL,7,FDiscussing the Birmingham bin strike
OL,8,Fwith BBC Radio WM, he says his party
OL,9,Fwould revisit the "crazy idea" that
OL,10,F"everybody has to be paid the same"
OL,12,FElsewhere, he discusses failing water
OL,13,Fcompanies with BBC Radio Kent, "slow"
OL,14,Fhousing planning with BBC Cornwall, and
OL,15,Fhis desire for a "positive vision for
OL,16,Fthe country" on BBC Radio Somerset
OL,18,FThe BBC local radio round has been a
OL,19,Fpre-conference tradition for many
OL,20,Fyears. Leaders of other major
OL,21,FWestminster parties have had a similar
OL,22,Fopportunity before their conferences
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
